                <div class="project-right">
                    <p>
                        I designed and developed a custom, Python-based algorithmic market scanner to monitor the Nasdaq-100 (QQQ) in real-time. The goal was to build a highly responsive intelligence pipeline that identifies high-probability options trading setups using live market data, without relying on delayed feeds or expensive premium subscriptions.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        To achieve real-time accuracy, the system leverages high-frequency REST polling via the Finnhub API. The incoming data streams are processed using Pandas, where an internal buffer calculates a 14-period Relative Strength Index (RSI) and a 5-period Simple Moving Average (SMA). This mathematical filtering strips out market noise and isolates true momentum breakouts.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        When the algorithmic conditions are met, the engine dynamically calculates the relevant Zero Days to Expiration (0DTE) strike prices based on the underlying spot price. To ensure seamless communication, the bot formats this intelligence into a professional JSON payload and dispatches it directly to a secure Discord server via Webhooks.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <em>This project required navigating complex network security constraints, handling asynchronous data handling to prevent buffer overflows, and deploying the final script as a continuous background service on a dedicated local edge node.</em>
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

